# 63. Question 9

What happens here?

```java
interface A {
    default void test() {
        System.out.println("A");
    }
}

interface B {
    default void test() {
        System.out.println("B");
    }
}

class C implements A, B {
}
```

Answer:

Compilation error due to conflicting default methods.

`C` must override:

```java
